A bad entry no longer turns a whole file into one error tiddler: the other entries are imported, and "BibTeX import error" lists the line and problem of each bad one. A file ending in a `%` line without a final newline no longer hangs the import.

The importer also accepts `@string` macros, parentheses around an entry, entries without fields, missing commas, whitespace before the comma after a citation key, and `@` signs in text between entries. Files that imported before give the same result as before.

New additions:

* With `$:/config/BibTeX/Standard` set to `yes`, the importer follows BibTeX's own brace rules and converts field values to plain text, so `{ACM}` becomes `ACM` and `M{\"u}ller` becomes `Müller`. It is off by default
* A "BibTeX" tab in the search results searches all fields of imported entries. It appears whenever the plugin is installed
* `{{Dalgaard2001||citeAPA}}` shows `(Dalgaard, 2001)` as a link to the entry
